  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the position vector of the point $P(-1,0,1)$ is $r(\\pi )=-i+\\,k.$\n\nThe osculating plane passes through the point that is at the tip of the vector $r(1).$ The vectors $T(1)$ and $N(1)$ are parallel to this plane. Therefore, the equation of the plane (in parametric form) can be written as\n\n$$\nR(s,u)=r(\\pi )+s\\,T(\\pi )+u\\,N(\\pi ),\\,s,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the equation of the osculating plane at the point $(-1,0,1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s,u) & =r(\\pi )+s\\,T(\\pi )+u\\,N(\\pi ) \\\\  & =(-i+\\,k)+s(\\frac{3}{5}\\,i-\\frac{4}{5}k)+u(-\\,j) \\\\  & =(-1+\\frac{3}{5}s)\\,i-u\\,j+(1-\\frac{4}{5}s)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
